        "lens": "reliability",
        "location": "scripts/h7-contract.mjs:19",
        "severity": "BLOCKER",
        "claim": "The H7 validator checks only that Cache-Control is marked x-required, so a contract mutation that changes its allowed value from no-store to a cacheable value is silently accepted. It also never validates the export's required Content-Disposition, X-Content-Type-Options, or Content-Type values. This leaves the frozen administrative-report and CSV response-header behavior unprotected despite those exact headers being an explicit security and reliability requirement.",
